            <ArticleTitle>Children with acute abdominal pain. Taking a reasonable approach.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1461-2, 1465-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Dealing with children with acute abdominal pain is often difficult for family physicians. This article attempts to set out a reasonable, step-progressive, and logical approach to this clinical situation. Emphasis is placed on the practical aspects of the situation and the need for the child to be involved in the examination.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
